  <prompt>Implement H0.5 as (a) a NEW BFF endpoint POST /api/onboarding/consent-callback (Anonymous, HMAC-verified) that captures the customer admin's tid on Microsoft admin-consent grant, seeds run parameters, and kicks the pipeline via Service Bus enqueue to the L2 control plane; and (b) an IJobHandler in the L2 control-plane that owns the re-consent semantics (no-op with 200+link if an active run exists for the same tid; restart from H0 if Failed/Cancelled). Idempotency key: consent-{customerId}-{tid}.</prompt>

  <role>SPAARKE platform developer. Expert in ASP.NET Core Minimal APIs, HMAC-SHA256 request signing, Anonymous endpoints (no AAD), ADR-013 PublicContracts facade, and CLAUDE.md §10 BFF Hygiene binding rule. Follow ADRs strictly.</role>

  <goal>Two new files exist: (1) src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Endpoints/Onboarding/ConsentCallbackEndpoint.cs — a Minimal API endpoint that verifies HMAC signature, extracts tid claim, seeds ProvisioningRun.parameters, enqueues to L2 via Service Bus, returns 202 Accepted (&lt;100ms). (2) src/server/services/Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane/Handlers/H05ConsentCaptureHandler.cs — an IJobHandler that owns re-consent semantics (no-op with 200 + existing run link if an active run has same tid + status ∈ {Ready, Running, WaitingOnGate}; restart from H0 if Failed/Cancelled). Endpoint is registered in Sprk.Bff.Api Program.cs; handler is registered in L2 DI. Unit tests cover HMAC verify (valid + invalid), Anonymous route wiring, re-consent branches, and idempotency.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>Per spec.md FR-02, design.md §4.1 H0.5 row, D18: Model 2 self-service requires ONE irreducible customer-tenant admin action (Microsoft admin-consent grant). The consent redirect page POSTs the callback to BFF with the customer tenant's tid claim. This is the ONLY BFF endpoint that must be Anonymous (customer admin is authenticating to THEIR tenant, not to Spaarke's control plane per §4.3a.2). BFF forwards to L2 for handler execution.</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="new">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Endpoints/Onboarding/ConsentCallbackEndpoint.cs</file>
      <file role="new">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Endpoints/Onboarding/HmacSignatureVerifier.cs</file>
      <file role="new">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Endpoints/Onboarding/ConsentCallbackEndpoint.Tests.cs</file>
      <file role="new">src/server/services/Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane/Handlers/H05ConsentCaptureHandler.cs</file>
      <file role="new">src/server/services/Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane/Handlers/H05ConsentCaptureHandler.Tests.cs</file>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Program.cs</file>
      <file role="modify">src/server/services/Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane/Program.cs</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/Registration/</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">.claude/patterns/auth/spaarke-sso-binding.md</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies>
      <dependency task="036" status="pending">L2 project scaffold (DI + JWT bearer + Cosmos + Service Bus wiring) — Wave C3</dependency>
    </dependencies>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="ADR-004">The L2-side handler is a single IJobHandler implementation — one message, one handler, one outcome.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-010">The BFF endpoint is placed in a dedicated Endpoints/Onboarding/ folder; DI additions are strictly bounded (single endpoint + HMAC verifier per spec.md ADR Tensions row ADR-010).</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-013">The consent-callback endpoint and handler MUST NOT inject IActionResolver / IActionRunner / IOpenAiClient / IPlaybookService directly. H0.5 is pure consent-capture — no AI needed. If future AI is required, invoke via Services/Ai/PublicContracts/ facade (per r3 task 040 forcing-functions ArchTest).</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-028">The endpoint is deliberately Anonymous (§4.3a.2) — the customer admin authenticates to their OWN tenant via the Microsoft consent flow, not to Spaarke's control plane. HMAC signing key is a shared secret stored as a KV URI ref in platform KV.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-036">The BFF endpoint enqueues to Service Bus and returns 202 Accepted &lt;100ms; the L2 handler executes off-thread. No synchronous handler execution in the HTTP request path (spec.md FR-22 / R20 / §4.2 fire-and-forget).</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Re-consent semantics per spec.md FR-02 + design.md §4.1 H0.5 row: if sprk_dataverseenvironment row exists with same tid + status ∈ {Ready, Running, WaitingOnGate}, return 200 + link to existing run (no-op); if Failed/Cancelled, restart from H0.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Idempotency key format `consent-{customerId}-{tid}` — tid is the customer tenant claim, NOT the operator's tid.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">spec.md §4D I1: NO hardcoded default tenant — every downstream Azure call parameterizes tenantId explicitly with the captured tid.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">spec.md NFR-05 + r3 task 061: if H0.5 introduces any new IOptions&lt;T&gt; (e.g., OnboardingOptions with HmacSigningKey), it MUST be classified per Tier 1/2/3 and either validated-on-start (Tier 1) or added to the Tier-2 exemption list per task-061-config-validation-classification.md.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">spec.md NFR-01: report BFF publish size + delta in the PR description. Baseline 44.96 MB incl PDBs; H0.5 endpoint expected delta &lt; 0.1 MB.</constraint>
    <constraint source="CLAUDE.md §10">Load .claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md before designing this addition. Placement Justification (Onboarding endpoint) MUST be stated in PR description per §10 bullet 2.</constraint>
  </constraints>

