  <steps mode="prescriptive">
    <step order="0">Declare rigor level (FULL) and load .claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md before designing. Load all knowledge files.</step>
    <step order="1">Run /conflict-check against active BFF worktrees before touching Sprk.Bff.Api.</step>
    <step order="2">Author HmacSignatureVerifier.cs — HMAC-SHA256 over the raw request body with signing key from IOptions&lt;OnboardingOptions&gt;. Constant-time comparison. Unit tests for valid + invalid signatures.</step>
    <step order="3">Author ConsentCallbackEndpoint.cs — Minimal API MapPost("/api/onboarding/consent-callback"), .AllowAnonymous(), body binds ConsentCallbackRequest { tid, customerId, correlationId }, verifies HMAC, seeds ProvisioningRun.parameters via Service Bus enqueue, returns 202 Accepted with runId.</step>
    <step order="4">Register endpoint + HMAC verifier + OnboardingOptions in Sprk.Bff.Api Program.cs. Classify OnboardingOptions per Tier 1/2/3 (Tier 1 → ValidateOnStart).</step>
    <step order="5">Author H05ConsentCaptureHandler.cs in L2 — implement IJobHandler; inject ICosmosRunStore, IDataverseEnvironmentRegistryClient. Read sprk_dataverseenvironment by tid; branch on status; return existing-run-link OR restart-from-H0 accordingly.</step>
    <step order="6">Author idempotency-key generator: consent-{customerId}-{tid}.</step>
    <step order="7">Register H05ConsentCaptureHandler in L2 Program.cs DI.</step>
    <step order="8">Author unit tests: (a) endpoint HMAC verify happy + invalid, (b) endpoint returns 401 on unauthenticated actually-anonymous route (should be 200 on missing header→ verifier catches), (c) endpoint returns 400 on missing HMAC header, (d) handler re-consent no-op branch, (e) handler restart-from-H0 branch, (f) handler idempotency (second call = no-op).</step>
    <step order="9">Run dotnet build for BOTH Sprk.Bff.Api AND Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane; run dotnet test; verify green + zero analyzer warnings.</step>
    <step order="10">Run BFF publish-size check: `dotnet publish -c Release src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/ -o deploy/api-publish/`; record absolute + delta vs 44.96 MB baseline in task notes and PR description per spec.md NFR-01.</step>
    <step order="11">Update TASK-INDEX.md: change task 042 status from 🔲 to ✅.</step>
    <step order="12">Document any deviations in projects/customer-provisioning-orchestration-r1/notes/.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If the HMAC signing-key rotation strategy differs from platform KV `@Microsoft.KeyVault(...)` reference pattern (e.g., must be short-lived per-run), STOP and escalate per CLAUDE.md §6 rather than inventing a new secret-storage pattern.</trigger>
    <trigger>If Wave C6 ArchTests (I1 no-hardcoded-tenant, I5 per-tenant Graph tokens) flag any code path in this handler at Step 9.5 code-review, treat as blocker — the tid must flow through as an explicit parameter to every downstream Azure call, not defaulted.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <justification>
    <existing>No existing consent-callback endpoint in BFF (grep for "consent-callback" returns none). Closest neighbor is src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/Registration/ (user registration endpoints — different concern; no HMAC + AAD-protected, not Anonymous).</existing>
    <extension>No — Anonymous+HMAC pattern is not compatible with the AAD-protected Registration endpoints; different auth surface. Onboarding folder is the correct new placement per §10 endpoint organization.</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>Without this endpoint, Model 2 self-service is impossible — every Model 2 provisioning requires a manual operator ceremony to capture the customer's tid + kick the pipeline. Per spec.md § Placement Justification: "the callback IS the extension point" for the ONE irreducible customer-tenant admin action. Without it, all Model 2 acquisitions require operator handholding, breaking the D18 self-service promise.</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>

  <tools>
    <tool name="dotnet">Build and test .NET projects (BFF + L2)</tool>
    <tool name="terminal">Run shell commands</tool>
  </tools>

  <outputs>
    <output type="code">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Endpoints/Onboarding/ConsentCallbackEndpoint.cs</output>
    <output type="code">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Endpoints/Onboarding/HmacSignatureVerifier.cs</output>
    <output type="test">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Endpoints/Onboarding/ConsentCallbackEndpoint.Tests.cs</output>
