    <output type="test">src/server/services/Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane/Handlers/H05ConsentCaptureHandler.Tests.cs</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">Given a POST to /api/onboarding/consent-callback with a valid HMAC-SHA256 signature over the raw body, when the endpoint runs, then it returns 202 Accepted &lt;100ms with the created runId in the response body.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: POST with a missing X-Signature header returns 400 Bad Request with a distinct error code (not 500).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: POST with an invalid HMAC signature returns 401 Unauthorized (verifier failure), not an unhandled exception.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given a valid POST with tid = customer-tenant-id, when the endpoint runs, then tid is written to sprk_dataverseenvironment.sprk_tenantid AND ProvisioningRun.parameters.tenantId; no default tenant fallback anywhere.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Re-consent no-op: given sprk_dataverseenvironment row with same tid + status ∈ {Ready, Running, WaitingOnGate}, when H05ConsentCaptureHandler runs, then it returns 200 with the existing runId link and does NOT restart the pipeline.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Re-consent restart: given sprk_dataverseenvironment row with same tid + status ∈ {Failed, Cancelled}, when H05ConsentCaptureHandler runs, then it restarts the pipeline from H0 and returns the new runId.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Idempotency: two identical enqueues for the same customerId + tid — second call is a no-op (consent-{customerId}-{tid} idempotency key match).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">BFF publish size delta &lt; 0.5 MB (spec.md NFR-01); PR description reports absolute + delta.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Endpoint uses Services/Ai/PublicContracts/ facade if AI needed (spec.md ADR-013 row); ArchTest at Step 9.5 confirms no direct IActionResolver / IActionRunner / IOpenAiClient injection.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">dotnet build for BFF exits 0; dotnet build for L2 exits 0; dotnet test for BOTH exits 0; zero analyzer warnings (analyzers-as-errors per spec.md NFR-06).</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>Reference: spec.md FR-02 + FR-22 + NFR-01 + NFR-05; design.md §4.1 H0.5 row + §4.2 API surface + §4.3a.2 auth flow + D18 self-service. The Anonymous+HMAC pattern is a deliberate exception to §10 general auth rules — cite in PR description. Coordinate with Wave C6 ArchTests for tenant-isolation compliance (I1/I5).</notes>

